# Android Manifest Permissions for Foreground Service

Add these permissions to your `android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml`:

## 1. Add Permissions (inside `<manifest>` tag, before `<application>`):

```xml
<!-- ✅ NEW: Foreground Service Permissions -->
<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE" />
<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE_LOCATION" />
<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.WAKE_LOCK" />
<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.REQUEST_IGNORE_BATTERY_OPTIMIZATIONS" />

<!-- Existing permissions should remain -->
<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET" />
<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION" />
<!-- ... other existing permissions ... -->
```

## 2. Add Service Declaration (inside `<application>` tag):

```xml
<application>
  <!-- Existing configurations -->
  
  <!-- ✅ NEW: Foreground Service for Active Shift -->
  <service
    android:name="com.taxitime.driverv1.ForegroundService"
    android:foregroundServiceType="location"
    android:enabled="true"
    android:exported="false" />
  
  <!-- Existing activities and components -->
</application>
```

## 3. Why This is Needed:

- **FOREGROUND_SERVICE**: Allows app to run continuously when driver has active shift
- **FOREGROUND_SERVICE_LOCATION**: Specifically for location tracking during shift
- **WAKE_LOCK**: Prevents device from sleeping during active shift
- **REQUEST_IGNORE_BATTERY_OPTIMIZATIONS**: Asks user to whitelist app from battery optimization

## 4. What This Does:

✅ Keeps app running in background when driver has active shift  
✅ Shows persistent notification that driver is "On Shift"  
✅ Ensures driver never misses job assignments  
✅ Prevents Android from killing the app to save battery  
✅ Complies with Android 12+ foreground service requirements  

## 5. User Experience:

When driver starts shift:
- Persistent notification appears: "🚕 On Shift - Available for Jobs"
- App continues running even when minimized
- Location tracking continues in background
- Socket connection remains active

When driver ends shift:
- Notification disappears
- App can be closed normally
- Background processing stops

## 6. Note:

This configuration is REQUIRED for Android 12+ (API 31+) to run foreground services.
Without it, the app may be killed by the system, causing drivers to miss jobs.

